        "geology": "Composing the Coleharbor Formation, river sediments (sand and gravel). Pleistocene and Holocene.\r\n",
        "hydrology": null,
        "soils": "Coarse, loamy, over-sandy or sandy, skeletal, mixed, superactive, frigid. Typic Haplustolls.\r\n",
        "vegetation": "The prairie in the Northern Plains Domain contains a combination of short- and mid-stature grasses and is dominated by blue grama (Bouteloua gracilis) and green needle grass (Nassella viridula). [1] Tame grasses, legumes, and many species of wildflower are also present. [1] The five most abundant plant species at the site include: Kentucky bluegrass (Poa pratensis), quackgrass (Elymus repens), smooth brome (Bromus inermis), wormwood (Artemisia absinthium), and big bluestem (Andropogon gerardii). [1]"
      },
